{
  "description": "A diagnostic adapter for Self-EvolveRec that measures a trained recommender through a stable compatibility interface and generates an interpretation prompt grounded in measured metrics and their definitions.",
  "motivation": "Support diagnosis-driven model improvements while preserving fair comparison across four Amazon datasets and avoiding assumptions about unavailable reviews, item attributes, or simulator traits.",
  "implementation_notes": "Retain DiagnosisProbe(view, device), run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), and diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis). Access the trained network through view.model and adapt architecture-specific probes while preserving the supplied compatibility contract. Training batches contain sequence, positive, and negative tensors of shape B × L. Use only public histories, titles, descriptions, and timestamps. Supply full-catalog unseen-item recommendations to 20 real training users, five per category. Select models using macro-average validation HR@10 across all four categories under the pinned evaluator; exclude hidden test data.",
  "pseudocode": "class DiagnosisProbe(view, device):\n    run_full_diagnosis(train_loader):\n        preserve model training state\n        put view.model in evaluation mode\n        disable gradients\n        measure supported diagnostics from batches and available public data\n        restore model training state\n        return {metrics: measured_values, metric_definitions: definitions}\n\nfunction diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis):\n    include measured metrics and their definitions\n    identify unavailable information explicitly\n    request evidence-grounded interpretation and improvement hypotheses\n    return prompt\n\nFor each candidate:\n    train using the prescribed splits and seeds\n    run adapted diagnostics\n    generate full-catalog unseen-item recommendations for designated users\n    select using common macro validation HR@10",
  "originality": {
    "score": 3,
    "positive": "Combines a stable diagnostic interface with explicit evidence constraints and a shared evaluation objective.",
    "negative": "The description defines an integration contract rather than a new recommendation algorithm or diagnostic method."
  },
  "future_potential": {
    "score": 7,
    "positive": "Could support consistent diagnosis and iterative improvements across multiple recommender architectures.",
    "negative": "Usefulness depends on the quality of the implemented probes and whether their findings translate into validation gains."
  },
  "code_difficulty": {
    "score": 5,
    "positive": "The required interface and batch format are explicit, making a baseline adapter straightforward.",
    "negative": "Architecture changes require careful probe adaptation, correct model-state handling, and consistent training and inference implementations."
  }
}
